#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
  ~#goal: "Promote thin spw-selector.ts into a composable pattern-based selector algebra in src/seed/query/. Selectors use Spw's own sigils, braces, and wildcards — not string type names."
  ~#taste: "expressiveness, layering — moving selector logic from script-land to library-land"
}

^["stream"]{
  # Append entries chronologically. Never edit prior entries.
  >> [2026-02-27 05:39] observe — existing spw-selector.ts uses walkAST + two inline matchers (maybePathRef, maybeRootRef). 133 lines, no composability.
  >> [2026-02-27 05:39] observe — ONF normalization already maps sigils to registers: !, ~, @, ^, #, ., ?, =, &, *, $, %. Selector patterns can mirror this directly.
  >> [2026-02-27 05:39] decide — selectors will be TS-constructed pattern objects for now (not a string DSL). Serializable subset for lore-remote dispatch.
  >> [2026-02-27 05:39] decide — new code lives in src/seed/query/ to keep it portable and importable from extension/CLi/LSP.
}

^["open"]{
  ?[wildcard_semantics]: "Should $_ match *any* node or only explicit Wildcard nodes? Design says any node — confirm during implementation."
  ?[depth_syntax]: "Depth range syntax ($!_:0..2). Is this needed for commit 1-4 or deferred?"
  ?[serialize_format]: "JSON shape for serializable selectors over spw/select. { sigil, brace, modifier } vs pattern string?"
}

